<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Fallout on Zack Dot Zip</title><link>https://zack.zip/tags/fallout/</link><description>Build logs, prop teardowns, and long-form 3D printing and cosplay write-ups from a garage in Washington State.</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 05:24:26 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://zack.zip/tags/fallout/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Fallout Automatic Laser Rifle</title><link>https://zack.zip/p/fallout-automatic-laser-rifle/</link><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 05:24:26 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://zack.zip/p/fallout-automatic-laser-rifle/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="fallout-automatic-laser-rifle"&gt;Fallout Automatic Laser Rifle&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="decals--stencils"&gt;Decals &amp;amp; Stencils&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;One of the things I thought would really elevate this build would be to include game accurate decals on the laser. I had a pretty hard time finding resources on these, so I ended up making my own based on texture rips from the Fallout 4 HD pack.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="tools-used"&gt;Tools Used&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;h4 id="software"&gt;Software&lt;/h4&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This could be its own blog post, so I&amp;rsquo;ll keep the nerd shit short.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I started with the &lt;a href="https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/974"&gt;Bethesda Archive Extractor&lt;/a&gt; to dump out the DDS files, which look like this:&#10;&lt;img src="https://zack.zip/p/fallout-automatic-laser-rifle/AssaultBarrel_d_hu_82edc630f639b574.webp" width="4096" height="4096" srcset="https://zack.zip/p/fallout-automatic-laser-rifle/AssaultBarrel_d_hu_cf923755f815a15b.webp 480w, https://zack.zip/p/fallout-automatic-laser-rifle/AssaultBarrel_d_hu_82edc630f639b574.webp 1024w, https://zack.zip/p/fallout-automatic-laser-rifle/AssaultBarrel_d_hu_81260044b031370.webp 2000w" sizes="(max-width: 720px) 100vw, 672px" data-full="/p/fallout-automatic-laser-rifle/AssaultBarrel_d_hu_81260044b031370.webp" data-ratio="1" alt="Triple Barrel Laser Texture" loading="lazy" decoding="async"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;From there a series of python and machine learning libraries were used to isolate, clean up, and export the decals, running locally in my lab environment:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;div class="chroma"&gt;&#10;&lt;table class="lntable"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 1&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 2&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 3&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 4&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 5&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 6&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 7&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 8&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt; 9&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="lnt"&gt;10&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&#10;&lt;td class="lntd"&gt;&#10;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-fallback" data-lang="fallback"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;game textures (.dds/.png) ──┐&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;STL stencils ├─► measure (NumPy/SciPy/trimesh)&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;A4 reference PDF (Poppler) ──┘ │&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; ▼&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; rebuild as geometry (Shapely + fontTools)&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; │&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; ┌───────────────┼────────────────┐&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; ▼ ▼ ▼&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; curves-only SVG 600 DPI PNG weathered PNG&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt; (mm canvases) (cairosvg) (noise pipeline)&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The end results were fairly accurate to the texture rips, with some SVG cleanup happening directly in Inkscape to close bodies and make them stencil cutter friendly.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;</description></item></channel></rss>